<%# src/views/partials/gallery-tile.ejs — the single photo tile every photo
    grid renders (issue #952 AC1/AC2, "gallery parity"): the Shared Gallery's
    recent wall and grouped-preview sections, a guest's public profile, and
    "My Photos" all open the SAME tile — thumbnail linking into the feed at
    that photo — so the mark a tile wears never drifts per surface. Before
    this partial, the tile markup was hand-copied at three call sites
    (gallery.ejs's renderTile, public-profile.ejs, guest-home.ejs); a fourth
    copy was the failure mode this extraction closes off, not a style
    preference.

    The tile's own href/aria-label are built HERE, not by the caller (PR
    review of #952): every caller was hand-concatenating the identical
    '/feed?from=<id>&scope=<token>#photo-<id>' / 'View photo for <alt>'
    formulas, which is the exact copy-drift this partial exists to close off
    for the surrounding markup, just one layer further in. `scopeToken` is the
    caller's ALREADY-TOKENIZED '?scope=' value ('u<id>' | 't<id>' | 'm',
    from feed.scopeToken() — see feed.js and community.js), never a scope
    descriptor object and never hand-built from raw parts here or by a caller.

    A top-5 crowd-favorite photo wears its crown, top-left (issue #788); a
    photo holding a released task-badge rank wears its victory medal,
    bottom-left (issue #811/#893) — both marks are OPTIONAL lookups, so a
    caller that omits one (guest-home's bare "My Photos" tiles) gets a plain
    tile rather than a throw, the same guard idiom every lookup below uses.
    overlayCount/overlayHref (issue #251) are the grouped-preview "+N" scrim
    a gallery section's overflowing last tile shows in place of the medal,
    and take over the tile's link/aria-label while active — /gallery's
    grouped previews are the only caller that ever passes them.

    Locals:
      thumbPath    (required) — the submission's thumbnail path (rendered as
                   /thumbs/<thumbPath>).
      id           (required) — the submission id: keys the crownRank/
                   badgeVictory lookups below AND builds the tile's own feed
                   link (/feed?from=<id>...).
      alt          (required) — the <img>'s alt text; also seeds the tile's
                   own aria-label ("View photo for <alt>").
      scopeToken   (optional) — the feed's already-tokenized '?scope=' value
                   ('u<id>' | 't<id>' | 'm'), from feed.scopeToken() — never
                   built here or by the caller from raw parts. Falsy (the
                   default) omits the scope param entirely, an unscoped link.
      crownRank    (optional) — submission_id -> rank map (issue #788).
                   Defaults to {} (the crown matches nothing).
      crownGoldId  (optional) — the sole rank-1 submission id, or null.
                   Defaults to null (no gold treatment).
      badgeVictory (optional) — submission_id -> { rank, badge } map (issue
                   #811/#893). Defaults to {} (the medal matches nothing).
      overlayCount (optional) — truthy renders the "+N" scrim instead of the
                   medal, and repoints the tile at overlayHref / "See all
                   photos in this section" instead of its own href/aria-label.
                   Falsy (the default) renders the plain tile.
      overlayHref  (required when overlayCount is truthy) — where the "+N"
                   scrim links. %>
<% var crownRank = (typeof crownRank !== 'undefined' && crownRank) ? crownRank : {}; %>
<% var crownGoldId = (typeof crownGoldId !== 'undefined') ? crownGoldId : null; %>
<% var badgeVictory = (typeof badgeVictory !== 'undefined' && badgeVictory) ? badgeVictory : {}; %>
<% var overlayCount = (typeof overlayCount !== 'undefined') ? overlayCount : 0; %>
<% var scopeToken = (typeof scopeToken !== 'undefined' && scopeToken) ? scopeToken : null; %>
<% var href = '/feed?from=' + id + (scopeToken ? '&scope=' + scopeToken : '') + '#photo-' + id; %>
<% var ariaLabel = 'View photo for ' + alt; %>
<figure class="gallery-item">
  <a
    class="gallery-thumb-btn"
    href="<%= overlayCount ? overlayHref : href %>"
    aria-label="<%= overlayCount ? 'See all photos in this section' : ariaLabel %>"
  >
    <img
      class="gallery-thumb"
      src="/thumbs/<%= thumbPath %>"
      alt="<%= alt %>"
      loading="lazy"
      width="400"
      height="400"
    />
    <% if (!overlayCount && crownRank[id]) { %>
      <%- include('crowd-favorite-mark', {
            rank: crownRank[id],
            gold: crownGoldId !== null && id === crownGoldId
          }) %>
    <% } %>
    <% if (overlayCount) { %>
      <span class="tile-more">+<%= overlayCount %></span>
    <% } else if (badgeVictory[id]) { %>
      <%# The gallery tile carries no like-count overlay (issue #811): the
          only bottom-left mark a photo wears is its task-badge victory
          medal, when it has won one — rendering the actual badge won
          (issue #893), not a generic glyph. %>
      <%- include('badge-victory-mark', {
            rank: badgeVictory[id].rank,
            badge: badgeVictory[id].badge
          }) %>
    <% } %>
  </a>
</figure>
